"Its name comes from the story of the cow (verses 67–73): the Children of Israel were told to sacrifice a cow and kept asking needless questions. The lesson is to obey Allah sincerely without looking for excuses. The Prophet ﷺ said Satan flees from a house in which Al-Baqarah is recited (Muslim)."
