hist=[
"At-Tawbah was revealed in Madinah in the ninth year after the Hijrah, among the final surahs. It is the only surah without the Bismillah. 'Ali is reported to have explained that the Bismillah is a declaration of safety, while this surah opens with a declaration of disavowal. 'Uthman reported that its content resembled Al-Anfal, and the Prophet ﷺ did not say whether they were one surah (Tirmidhi).",
"Its opening was announced during the Hajj of 9 AH, led by Abu Bakr, with 'Ali proclaiming it: treaty-breaking idolaters had four months, after which no idolater would perform Hajj and no one would circle the Ka'bah naked.",
"Most of the surah concerns the expedition to Tabuk against the Byzantines, in intense summer heat and at harvest time. The hypocrites made excuses and stayed behind. Three sincere believers, Ka'b ibn Malik, Murarah ibn al-Rabi' and Hilal ibn Umayyah, also stayed behind without excuse. They were boycotted for fifty days until their repentance was accepted (Bukhari), and the surah takes its name from that repentance."
],
